  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Lifesaving Basic Service Provision for Drought and Flood affected IDPs  Host Communities of Bare Woreda in Afdher Zone of Somali Region of Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtlt/pgtltpgtltspangtAgriculture:
The agriculture intervention will focus on providing support to the
agricultural sector to help restore livelihoods and enhance food security. The
proposed activities include the provision of restocking small ruminants,
support for livestock vaccination and treatment, and cash-based interventions,
such as cash for work for the rehabilitation of range land and natural resource
management. The intervention will target approximately 10000 households (60000
people), benefiting them with enhanced livestock production and productivity.
Emergency livestock response areas, where IR has accumulated several years of
experience, and qualified staff who attended LEGS training and have been
implementing several similar projects in the past. Currently several emergency
livestock projects in Afder ( outside of Barey) and elsewhere.lt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspangt
ltbrgt
WaSH, through rehabilitation and upgrading to solar system one strategic and
linking with the water distribution system, distribution of WaSH NFI (Dual
purpose Soap) for three consecutive months,&#xa0;&#xa0;Construction of
gender-segregated latrines (4 blocks * 4 seats) for IDPs with no access
latrines, hygiene and Sanitation promotion for a total of eight months reaching
a total of&#xa0;31,531 people. The experience and expertise IRE has accumulated
over the year will help to implement the project effectively and efficiently.
IRE&#xa0;is one the lead organizations in the implementation of WaSH programmes in
the region and elsewherelt/spangtlt/pgt




ltpgtltbrgtProtection includes community capacity building on protection, basic child and GBV case management, and community awareness raising on protection.lt/pgtltpgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
